    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/dns/" class="hover:text-accent">DNS Guide</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">What Is DNS</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">What Is DNS?</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      DNS, the <strong class="text-ink">Domain Name System</strong>, is the internet's address book.
      People remember <code>promptdns.com</code>; computers connect to <code>104.21.x.x</code>. DNS is
      the system that translates between the two, billions of times per day, for every website visit
      and every email delivery.
    </p>
    </div>

    

    

    

    

    

    
